msgctxt "856"
msgid ""
"Amazing! Well done, my prized pupil! You executed a perfect Komaki Dragon "
"King Essence!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "868"
msgid "Whew... I did?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "880"
msgid ""
"Indeed! Why, it was just like looking into a mirror. You moved as fluidly "
"as I did at your young age!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "892"
msgid "Really? That's quite the compliment. Thank you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "904"
msgid "You learned <Color:9>Komaki Dragon King Essence<Color:Default>!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "952"
msgid ""
"With this, you have learned all of the techniques in the book. I have "
"nothing more to teach you, my dearest disciple."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "964"
msgid ""
"You will find it difficult to seek opponents who will truly challenge you "
"now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "976"
msgid ""
"But if you do, you must not lose! Remember this, my favorite student, as "
"you are now the successor of the Komaki school!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "988"
msgid "Don't worry, I won't. Thank you for everything, old man."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1000"
msgid "It was my pleasure."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1012"
msgid "I should probably get going. Thanks for all the help."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1024"
msgid ""
"I spend most of my time here, in the dojo. You may come see me any time you "
"feel your skills need polishing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1036"
msgid ""
"But of course, Kamurocho is a very small town. We may very well run into "
"one another somewhere. Who knows?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1048"
msgid "Glad to see you're still keeping active, old man. See you later."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1060"
msgid "Now then, it's time for you to learn the Heaven technique."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1072"
msgid "All right. Been looking forward to this one."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1084"
msgid ""
"It's called <Color:9>Komaki Dragon King Essence<Color:Default>. As I said "
"before, this can only be passed on from a master to his chosen pupil."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1108"
msgid "As such, I've asked my pupils to leave us alone."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1120"
msgid ""
"Komaki Dragon King Essence must be performed after using <Color:7>Komaki "
"Parry<Color:Default> to render your opponent unconscious."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1132"
msgid ""
"Komaki Parry? That's the move you can perform just as the opponent throws a "
"punch, right?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1144"
msgid ""
"I want you practice using this move in combat for this last lesson. "
"However, as I said, I've asked my pupils to step out..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1156"
msgid "Heh..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1168"
msgid "So, I'll be facing you, huh?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1180"
msgid "Hahaha! Precisely! Your final opponent will be none other than me!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1240"
msgid ""
"But know that I am not going to hold back. You will not be able to beat me "
"unless you come at me with all of your might. Now, let me see you perfect "
"the <Color:7>Komaki Dragon King Essence<Color:Default>!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1252"
msgid ""
"Hold <Action:Battle_Fight_Stance@Combat> to enter a fighting stance, then "
"press <Action:Battle_Drop_Weapon@Combat> when an enemy attacks with a bare "
"fist to perform a <Color:7>Komaki Parry<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1264"
msgid ""
"Afterwards, approach the unconscious enemy and press\r\n"
"<Action:Battle_Heavy_Attack@Combat> to perform a <Color:7>Komaki Dragon "
"King Essence<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1276"
msgid "Are you prepared? Then let us begin!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1300"
msgid "Are you ready to continue your training, my pupil?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1336"
msgid "I cannot teach you new techniques when someone is fighting alongside you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1348"
msgid "These techniques cannot be allowed into the hands of outsiders!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1360"
msgid ""
"Tsk, tsk, tsk! Come back to see me when you're alone. I'll be waiting for "
"you, my pupil!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1372"
msgid "Let us move on to your next lesson."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1384"
msgid "Very well. Let me know when you are ready."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1396"
msgid "Astounding!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1408"
msgid ""
"That was the perfect <Color:9>Komaki Bowl Crusher<Color:Default>! Few "
"people can remain standing after taking a hard hit like that to the head!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1420"
msgid "Bowl Crusher? Fitting name."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1432"
msgid "I bet I could handle even tougher enemies with this move in my repertoire."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1444"
msgid "You can now use <Color:9>Komaki Bowl Crusher<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1456"
msgid "You have now mastered two of the three secret techniques."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1468"
msgid "I never thought you would learn so fast."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1480"
msgid ""
"It's all thanks to you and your pupils. I would never have been able to do "
"it by myself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1492"
msgid "I suppose you're right... I am quite the impressive teacher, after all!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1504"
msgid "And you're modest, too..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1516"
msgid "Hey! That's no way to talk to your master!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1528"
msgid ""
"In any case, only one remains: the Heaven technique. Perhaps you'd like to "
"rest a bit before you attempt to master it?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1540"
msgid "Very well. Let me know when you are ready."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1576"
msgid "I'd like to continue with your training, but..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1588"
msgid "I cannot teach you new techniques when someone is fighting alongside you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1600"
msgid "These techniques cannot be allowed into the hands of outsiders!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1612"
msgid ""
"Tsk, tsk, tsk! Come back to see me when you're alone. I'll be waiting for "
"you, my pupil!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1624"
msgid "Let us move on to your next lesson."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1636"
msgid ""
"Next is the technique of Earth. To execute this technique, you must grab "
"hold of your opponent, then drop him on his head from a height."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1648"
msgid "But this technique won't do much damage without a proper object to land on."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1660"
msgid ""
"Try dropping them onto something around knee height for maximum "
"effectiveness."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1672"
msgid "Drop them down onto a short object... Got it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1696"
msgid "(That looks to be about the right height.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1708"
msgid ""
"There are limited options here in the dojo. Finding the best place to "
"perform this technique is a critical part of the learning process."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1720"
msgid "Now try it against my pupil, as before."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1732"
msgid "All right."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1768"
msgid ""
"Grab your opponent with your Heat Gauge full, and approach an object that "
"is around <Color:7>knee height<Color:Default>. Then, press "
"<Action:Battle_Heavy_Attack@Combat> to use this technique."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1780"
msgid "Are you ready?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1792"
msgid "Now... begin!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1816"
msgid "Are you ready to continue your training, my pupil?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1852"
msgid "I cannot teach you new techniques when someone is fighting alongside you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1864"
msgid "These techniques cannot be allowed into the hands of outsiders!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1876"
msgid ""
"Tsk, tsk, tsk! Come back to see me when you're alone. I'll be waiting for "
"you, my pupil!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1888"
msgid "Now, then. Let's continue your training."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1900"
msgid "Very well. Let me know when you are ready."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1912"
msgid "Astounding!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1924"
msgid ""
"Yes, that was indeed a <Color:9>Komaki Swordless Rebirth<Color:Default>.\r\n"
"Use this technique on a sword-wielding opponent to quickly turn the tables "
"on him!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1936"
msgid "Swordless Rebirth..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1948"
msgid ""
"This could be pretty useful. You never know what kinds of weapons guys are "
"walking around with nowadays."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1960"
msgid "You can now use <Color:9>Komaki Swordless Rebirth<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1972"
msgid ""
"Hmm... I'd like to go on to the next technique, but perhaps you would like "
"to rest a while before resuming your training."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1984"
msgid "Very well. Let me know when you are ready."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2020"
msgid "I'd like to continue with your training, but..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2032"
msgid "I cannot teach you new techniques when someone is fighting alongside you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2044"
msgid "These techniques cannot be allowed into the hands of outsiders!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2056"
msgid ""
"Tsk, tsk, tsk! Come back to see me when you're alone. I'll be waiting for "
"you, my pupil!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2068"
msgid "Let us move on to your next lesson."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2080"
msgid "Hey, I found that book you wanted. Here you go."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2092"
msgid ""
"Well done, my favorite pupil! I didn't expect you to be able to find it so "
"quickly!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2104"
msgid "Let's get right to it then, and continue your training!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2140"
msgid "However, as much as I would like to do just that..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2152"
msgid "I cannot teach you new techniques when someone is fighting alongside you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2164"
msgid "These techniques cannot be allowed into the hands of outsiders!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2176"
msgid ""
"Tsk, tsk, tsk! Come back to see me when you're alone. I'll be waiting for "
"you, my pupil!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2188"
msgid "Sure, I'm ready."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2200"
msgid ""
"There are three skills to learn from this book: the techniques of Heaven, "
"Earth, and Man."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2212"
msgid ""
"Of particular note is the Heaven technique, the most secretive of all, that "
"a master must only convey upon his chosen pupil."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2224"
msgid ""
"Before Heaven, we must learn the Man and Earth techniques. First, let's "
"begin with Man."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2236"
msgid "Sounds good."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2248"
msgid "To use the Man technique, your opponent must be armed with a bladed weapon."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2260"
msgid "So I can only use it when someone's coming at me with a sword or something?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2272"
msgid ""
"Just so. If you are able to use it successfully, however, you may be able "
"to turn the tables on your opponent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2284"
msgid "Try it on my pupil over there."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2296"
msgid "All right."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2332"
msgid "Hi, Kiryu-san. Please take it easy on me."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2344"
msgid ""
"Your opponent must be holding a sword. With the Heat Gauge full, press "
"<Action:Battle_Heavy_Attack@Combat> at the same time the enemy attacks you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2356"
msgid "Are you ready?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2368"
msgid "Now... begin!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2392"
msgid "Oho, if it isn't Kiryu. You still haven't found that book, I see."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2428"
msgid "Kamekichi should be in a park somewhere in Kamurocho."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2440"
msgid "Kamekichi sometimes stops by the gambling halls."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2452"
msgid ""
"One of my pupils did say they saw a strange-looking book being sold at a "
"shop somewhere..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2464"
msgid "What would you like to know, my pupil?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2476"
msgid "Kiryu... Do you know what the word \"bounding\" means?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2488"
msgid "Bounding? Not sure I've heard of it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2500"
msgid ""
"It is the act of unleashing an attack that sends someone flying against the "
"ground or wall, causing them to bounce, or \"bound.\""
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2512"
msgid ""
"Bounding can mean the difference between victory and defeat. If your timing "
"is just right, you can sneak in an additional hit on your opponent. This is "
"especially true for wall bounding."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2524"
msgid ""
"If you hit an opponent with an attack that sends him flying, they will "
"bound off the ground or a wall. Use that brief moment to strike once again. "
"If you're too far from the wall, or the enemy cannot be downed, then you "
"will not be able to hit them again."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2536"
msgid ""
"Some types of weapon attacks can make it easier to perform a bounding "
"attack. Continue to practice, and you will find yourself mastering the "
"skill before long."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2548"
msgid ""
"Kiryu, my dear pupil... Do you know how to grab an opponent that has been "
"downed?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2560"
msgid "Wait, you can do that?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2572"
msgid ""
"What!? You don't!? I can't believe you've survived as long as you have "
"without knowing such an essential skill. We'll have to chalk it up to your "
"exceptional luck."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2584"
msgid "...I think you might be exaggerating a bit, old man."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2596"
msgid ""
"Quiet! Listen, now. When your opponent is down, you can either grab him by "
"the leg or force him to stand up."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2608"
msgid ""
"Try grabbing a downed opponent near his feet. Then, you can either attack "
"him or throw him. There are also some special moves you can only use on a "
"downed opponent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2620"
msgid ""
"If you grab him near his head, you can force him to stand up again. This is "
"particularly useful against opponents who are vulnerable to combination "
"attacks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2632"
msgid ""
"Instead of simply attacking a downed opponent, you can grab them by the leg "
"if you are by their feet, or force them to stand up if you are by their "
"head."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2644"
msgid "Remember this skill, my pupil, as it may serve you well someday."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2656"
msgid ""
"Kiryu, my dear pupil... Do you know why certain opponents will sometimes "
"writhe about on the ground?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2668"
msgid "I just figured they were in pain. Does it mean something special?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2680"
msgid ""
"Something special indeed. This behavior is only exhibited by weaker "
"opponents. When they are downed with less than half their health remaining, "
"they will writhe about on the ground."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2692"
msgid ""
"Each opponent will only do this once. When you see him writhe about instead "
"of getting up right away, you can choose to finish him off or face other "
"enemies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2704"
msgid ""
"However, if you force an opponent in this state to stand up, he will fall "
"unconscious. You can do this by standing near his head and grabbing him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2716"
msgid ""
"When an opponent goes down with less than half their health remaining, they "
"will writhe about on the ground. This will only occur once per enemy. Force "
"them to stand up to render them unconscious."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2728"
msgid ""
"This skill can be quite useful, as there are some moves you can only use on "
"an unconscious opponent. Continue to practice, and you will master this "
"skill before long."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2740"
msgid "Kiryu, my dear pupil... Have you heard of the Recovery Stance?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2752"
msgid "Don't think I have."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2764"
msgid ""
"The Recovery Stance is a term used in martial arts. When you are in "
"Recovery Stance, you do not relax, even if your enemy is down on the ground."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2776"
msgid "...So it's some kind of special mental state, then?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2788"
msgid ""
"Let me finish. This stance is not just a question of concentration or "
"mental discipline. No, my dear pupil, it is far more than that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2800"
msgid ""
"When you use certain attacks, you can fall into the Recovery Stance. Doing "
"so will help to fill you with fighting spirit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2812"
msgid ""
"Enter Recovery Stance by holding down <Action:Battle_Heavy_Attack@Combat> "
"when using certain attacks, such as the fourth hit in an unarmed combo."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2824"
msgid ""
"This will let you build up Heat, but leave you unable to move and "
"vulnerable to enemy attacks. Recovery Stance can be used with many "
"different moves and skills⑬give it a try!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2836"
msgid ""
"If you learn when and where to enter Recovery Stance, you can earn extra "
"Heat, making it easier to execute critical blows. Continue to practice, and "
"you will master it before long."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2848"
msgid "Come back to see me whenever you like, my prized pupil."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2860"
msgid "Well, if it isn't my favorite pupil! What can I do for you today?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2896"
msgid "Hmm..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2908"
msgid "I cannot teach you new techniques when someone is fighting alongside you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2920"
msgid "These techniques cannot be allowed into the hands of outsiders!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2944"
msgid "I was hoping you could teach me a new move or two."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2968"
msgid ""
"Your enthusiasm is admirable, but I don't have any new moves for you right "
"now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2980"
msgid "You need more practice and more experience."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2992"
msgid ""
"(Guess he can't teach me anything new right now. I should work on getting "
"more experience...)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3004"
msgid ""
"Oho! You certainly do possess an impressive amount of strength. Now, what "
"technique would be appropriate for a man like you..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3016"
msgid "Hmm..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3028"
msgid "Hrm..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3040"
msgid ""
"I've got it! There are three secret techniques that have been passed down "
"from master to pupil for centuries. I can think of none more fitting for "
"you, my dear pupil!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3052"
msgid "How I wish I could teach them to you now..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3064"
msgid "What, you can't? Why not?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3076"
msgid ""
"Teaching the techniques themselves is no problem⑬I know them like the back "
"of my own hand. The problem lies in the tradition of teaching these "
"techniques."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3088"
msgid ""
"The secret tome that describes these techniques is missing, and it must be "
"passed on to whomever learns them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3100"
msgid "A book? How did you manage to lose something that important?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3112"
msgid ""
"A homeless man ran off with it during the confusion of moving all of our "
"materials into the Dragon Palace."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3124"
msgid ""
"We were all so preoccupied, we didn't realize what had happened until it "
"was too late."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3136"
msgid ""
"If you can find the book and bring it to me, I can teach you those secret "
"techniques."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3148"
msgid "Another errand to add to the pile, I suppose."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3160"
msgid "It's not an errand! This is part of your training!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3172"
msgid "All right, all right. Where can I find this homeless man?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3184"
msgid "Hmm..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3196"
msgid ""
"His name is Kamekichi. From what I hear, he spends a lot of time in a park. "
"There are several parks in Kamurocho, so you may need to take a look around."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3208"
msgid "All right. I'll go see if I can find him."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3220"
msgid "Good luck. If you find that book, come back and see me!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3232"
msgid "Kiryu... Do you know what the word \"bounding\" means?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3244"
msgid "Bounding? Not sure I've heard of it."
msgstr ""

